etector ran cleanly and on attempts written before PRD 00077). The `"escalated"` outcome value is stamped on the entry for a rung the task was reset away from and escalated up; the final rung's entry carries the real terminal outcome (`completed`/`aborted`), and the escalated-away entry keeps its true `implementor` (a qwen rung escalated to Sonnet keeps `implementor:"qwen"`; likewise, a codex attempt records `model` at the task's own tier, e.g. `"sonnet"`, with `implementor: "codex"` carrying the backend identity — the same split the qwen rung already uses). **Micro-lane fields (PRD 00148, both optional):** `implementor` gains `"orchestrator"` — the one value meaning no implementor dispatched at all, stamped when a small rework task was edited in-session by the orchestrator (`work/references/rework-mode.md` § Micro lane), which also records `red_check: "n/a:micro-lane"`. `micro_lane` (string?; `"overrun"` when the lane's post-edit ceiling fired, the edit was reverted and the task fell through to a normal dispatch — that attempt records the real dispatcher in `implementor`; absent otherwise). `reflow` (string?; `"<path>:<hunks>"`, `;`-joined for several, when `/autopilot:work` step 5's `check_reflow.py` flagged a staged file, or `"failed:<stderr>"` when the script could not run; absent when nothing was flagged). **Per-task review field (PRD 00159):** `review` (string?; `"failed:<cause>"` when the step-5.7 reviewer lane failed twice, `"failed:invalid_output"` when both replies broke the reporting contract and `parse_review.py` rejected each, `"skipped:test-only"` when every path in `<task_base_sha>..HEAD` was test or fixture code outside rework mode; may also carry a `medium-retry:fixed`/`medium-retry:unfixed` suffix from PRD 00140. Absent when the review ran cleanly or the haiku tier-gate skipped it). **Per-task style gate (PRD 00163):** `style_gate` (string?; the step-5.65 verdict on that task's own diff — `"clean"`, `"fixed:<sha>"` (one fix dispatch landed and the 